              Claude Commander (cc) -- Keyboard Help

  NAVIGATION
    Up/Down ......... move cursor          Tab ........... switch panel
    PgUp/PgDn ....... page                 Home/End ...... top / bottom
    Enter ........... open dir / run       Backspace ..... parent dir
    Insert .......... tag / untag entry

  FUNCTION KEYS
    F1 .. this help          F3 .. view          F4 .. edit (CCEDIT)
    F5 .. copy*              F6 .. move*          F7 .. make dir
    F8 .. delete             F9 .. menu           F10 . quit
    *to the OTHER panel; the dialog lets you rename in flight. Shift-F6
     renames in place (same folder). F2 is unused.
    F9 / menu bar ... pull-down menus Files / Commands / Options / Tools.
                      F9 drops the current menu; Left/Right switch menus,
                      Up/Down pick, Enter runs, Esc closes. Or click a title,
                      then an item (click outside closes). CCPOP.COM has the
                      classic single pop-up menu instead.
    Tools menu ...... Hex dump (F3 pager in hex), Checksum (CCSUM CRC-32),
                      Compare (CCDIFF, this vs other panel's file), Split
                      file (CCSPLIT, asks piece size), Wildcard rename (CCREN,
                      asks masks). CCUSER.COM appends cc.ini [tools] rows,
                      run as "<program> <cursor-file>" (.BAT gets it as %1;
                      see TOOLSAMP).
    Alt-F1/F2 ....... drive list in the left / right panel; Enter opens a
                      drive's root, Esc (or "..") returns to the prior folder
    Alt-F5 .......... pack tagged/cursor into an archive in the other panel
                      (tagged folders recurse)
    Alt-F7 .......... find files by name (CCFIND); matches fill the other
                      panel as a list; Enter jumps to that file's folder
    Alt-F8 .......... grep file contents (CCGREP); the other panel lists one
                      row per matching file (first-match line in the size
                      column); Enter opens the F3 viewer at that line.
                      Leave a results list with Esc or ".." (like a ZIP).
    Alt-F9 .......... extract a whole archive to the other panel
    Alt-F10 ......... directory tree under the active panel's path: cursor
                      keys move, Enter jumps the panel there, Esc cancels

  VIEWERS (the [view] map in cc.ini selects a viewer per extension)
    F3 on a mapped file runs "<viewer> <file>" (e.g. [view] gif = CCIMG);
    others use the built-in pager: cursor keys scroll, H toggles TEXT / HEX
    dump (offset, 16 bytes, ASCII), Esc or F3 quits. E edits the file: TEXT
    mode opens the configured editor (see CONFIG), HEX mode opens CCHEXED;
    cc reloads the file afterwards.
    CCIMG <file> .... bmp/pcx/gif (VGA 13h); any key / Esc returns
    CCWAV <file> .... PCM .wav via the Sound Blaster; any key / Esc returns
    CCMDL <file> .... Quake .mdl 3D viewer: arrows rotate, Space spins,
                      A animates, N/P step frames, Esc/Q/F3 quit

  ARCHIVES (the [open] map in cc.ini selects a packer per extension)
    Enter on an archive browses it like a folder; F5 extracts the cursor
    member, Alt-F9 every member, to the other panel.
    .zip ............ sub-folders included (paths kept); ".." goes up,
                      Backspace leaves at the top. With the OTHER panel
                      inside a .zip, F5 ADDS tagged/cursor files (recursive)
    .d64 / .t64 ..... C64 1541 disk / tape image; files extract as
                      <name>.PRG (.t64 restores the load address)
    .arj / .rar ..... ARJ / RAR 4.x: only STORED members extract (compressed
                      ones are listed, not decoded)
    .pak ............ Quake PAK, sub-folders included (paths kept); F3 on a
                      member opens its [view] helper without extracting
                      (a .mdl opens straight in CCMDL)

  DISPLAY / SELECT
    Ctrl-F1..F4 ..... sort by name / ext / size / date
    Ctrl-F5 ......... cycle column: size / date / time / attributes
    Ctrl-F6 ......... incremental quick-search
    Ctrl-F7/F8 ...... tag / untag files by *.mask
    Ctrl-A .......... edit attributes (Read-only/Hidden/System/Archive)
    Ctrl-F9 ......... list archive contents (CCZIP)
    Ctrl-F10 ........ cycle the panel view (per panel): full list -> brief
    (Alt-F3 DOSBox)   3-column names -> LFN long-name view (long names with
                      an LFN provider, else 8.3). In brief view Left/Right
                      move between columns. Also on the Options menu.
    Panel footer .... "<n> Files <free>K free", or "<n> selected <total>
                      bytes" once files are tagged; the clock ticks each
                      second
    Long names ...... with an LFN provider (Win9x DOS / DOSLFN) the cursor
                      file's long name shows on the command row

  EXTERNAL TOOLS (type the name at the prompt, then Enter)
    CCHEX <file> .... hex + ASCII dump of any file
    CCHEXED <file> .. overwrite-only hex editor: arrows move, hex digits
                      overwrite, F2 saves, Esc quits (also the hex view's E)
    CCSUM <file> .... CRC-32 + byte size (verify two files match)
    CCGREP w d m .... search file contents (also Alt-F8)
    CCFIND p d ...... find files by name (also Alt-F7)
    CCZIP <zip> ..... list a ZIP archive (also Ctrl-F9)
    CCDIFF f1 f2 .... byte-compare two files (offset of first difference)
    CCSPLIT f n[K] .. split a file into f.001, f.002, ... of n bytes each
    CCJOIN out base . rejoin base.001, base.002, ... into one file
    CCREN src dst ... wildcard multi-rename, e.g. CCREN *.TXT *.BAK
    CCTOUCH <file> [YYYY-MM-DD [HH:MM[:SS]]]
                      set a file's date/time (no date = now)

  CONFIG
    cc.ini .......... initial "sort" and "columns"; clock position (clock =
                      cmdrow | topright | off); the F4 editor: editor =
                      CCEDIT (default) | EDIT | CCHEXED | any program on
                      the PATH. CCUSER.COM [tools] lines: Label = PROG [key]
                      e.g. File info = INFO.BAT Shift-F3
    cc.lng .......... translate the F-key bar (copy da.lng to cc.lng)

  Scroll with Up/Down/PgUp/PgDn; press Esc, q, F1, F3 or F10 to close.
